----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Same algorithm, independent expression (SonicBoom's own; no ggml code copied)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

These reproduce ggml's *behavior* (bit-for-bit where the comment says so) but
are written independently and are not derived works:

  - core/src/quant/dequant.cpp     q3/q4/q5_K dequantize (independent C++23;
                                   header already notes ggml is MIT-licensed)
  - core/src/nn/activation.cpp     gelu_tanh_f32 / gelu_fp16 (standard tanh
                                   GELU formula from the original paper)
  - core/src/nn/norm.cpp           rms_norm (standard rms-norm formula)
  - core/src/nn/matmul.cpp         matvec_bf16 (standard bf16 inner product)
  - half_to_float (GGML_FP16_TO_FP32 semantics)  IEEE 754 binary16→binary32
  - core/src/quant/quantized_matmul.cpp  AVX2 q8_K dot kernels
  - core/src/quant/cuda_quant_matmul.cu   fp32 gemv_q*_K_base/_coop kernels

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Format reference only (not derived code)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

The GGUF reader and the quantized-tensor table
(core/src/quant/quantized_tensor.cpp, core/include/sonicboom/quant/quantized_tensor.h)
re-declare ggml's numeric *type ids* and the block-quantized *layouts* so they can
parse GGUF files. These are data-format constants and structure layouts, not a
derived implementation of ggml code.
